(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The compiled code: each closure's body a tree of nodes over the slots of its frame (its free"] [11 1 "// variables first, then its arguments, then every local binder of the body, join points' arguments"] [12 1 "// among them). A node's eval returns the next node to run in a frame (a tail position), or nil when it"] [13 1 "// has put its value in the machine's return registers."] [18 1 "// Atom is an argument: a slot, a global or a literal."] [20 13 "// aSlot, aGlobal, aLit"] [46 1 "// val is get with a slot's read inline (the frequent kind)."] [62 1 "// scope is a closure's compile-time frame."] [69 2 "// tail: the expression compiled is in its function's tail position, outside every case's scrutinee: no frame of"] [70 2 "// the activation is on the stack there, so a call may reuse the activation's frame (App.tail)"] [72 2 "// atail: the expression is in its activation's tail position (outside every scrutinee), in a function or a thunk:"] [73 2 "// a call or an entry there clears the activation's local slots, dead from then on, so a frame the stack still holds"] [74 2 "// (a thunk evaluated in its own array, an arena's frame) keeps nothing alive (App.clr, Enter.clr); nfree its"] [75 2 "// closure's free variables, which stay (a thunk reverted needs them)"] [98 1 "// bind gives name a fresh slot; the returned func restores the outer binding."] [124 1 "// isVoid reports a binder's representations of none (:v)."] [139 1 "// atom compiles an argument."] [179 3 "// two's complement truncation"] [187 1 "// literal is a literal's value (STG-SPEC §5)."] [257 1 "// staticCon is the one value of a constructor whose fields are all literals (as GHC's static closures: immutable,"] [258 1 "// so one value serves every evaluation), or nil. Not in an image's compilation: its literals may be placeholders."] [280 1 "// rubbish is a LitRubbish of a lifted or unlifted type: never entered."] [283 1 "// literal keys of case alternatives: integers by their 64 bits, floats as themselves."] [292 1 "// compileLambda compiles (closure UPD [FREE...] [BINDER...] EXPR) in a frame of its own."] [302 3 "// a function's (or a re-entrant closure's) frame holds copies of its free variables: cleared with the rest"] [303 3 "// (queue 446: forkIO's catch# kept its action, the thread's whole loop, in its frame's free slot)"] [322 1 "// freeAtoms are a closure's free variables as atoms of the enclosing frame."] [332 1 "// expr compiles an expression. minDouble#'s and maxDouble#'s (and Float#'s) literal operand goes second:"] [333 1 "// GHC's code generator emits minsd reg, [lit], and the operands' order decides a NaN's and a zero's result."] [375 4 "// GHC's code generator puts a literal operand second (minsd reg, [lit]): the order decides"] [376 4 "// a NaN's and a zero's result"] [413 3 "// a literal"] [420 1 "// isTuple reports an unboxed tuple's constructor (returned as several values, STG-SPEC §3)."] [499 1 "// let compiles (let BIND EXPR): closures and constructors allocated in the frame's slots."] [561 1 "// letne compiles join points: their arguments are slots of this frame, a jump assigns them."] [600 2 "// the join points' bodies see each other (rec) and themselves"] [622 2 "// (ffi TARGET CONV SAFETY [ATOM...] REPS)"] [643 4 "// the I/O manager's question (threaded.go): hsi's I/O manager is the non-threaded RTS's in both ways"] [653 1 "// ioManagerThreaded is the pseudo-symbol rtsSupportsBoundThreads compiles to outside boundThreadsAsker's modules: 0, the"] [654 1 "// I/O manager hsi has (threaded.go)."] [657 1 "// boundThreadsAsker reports a binding of a module whose rtsSupportsBoundThreads asks about bound threads (forkOS,"] [658 1 "// isCurrentThreadBound, runInBoundThread: GHC.Internal.Conc.Bound) or is the program's own, not about the I/O manager"] [659 1 "// (GHC.Internal.Conc.IO, Event.Thread, IO.FD, System.Timeout, the signals' modules)."] [668 1 "// cSymbol is the C function a static target calls: a capi wrapper's name decoded"] [669 1 "// (ghczuwrapperZC23ZC...ZCread is read)."] [679 1 "// zdecode decodes GHC's z-encoding of a name."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[143 25] [340 26] [383 28] [384 43] [397 25] [476 23] [476 31] [555 22] [555 30] [610 24] [610 32] [615 22] [615 30] [628 23] [662 34] [672 39] [682 12] [682 24] [726 22]]} (go/file "compile.go" :imports [


